"""Privileged backend of the Configuration page.

read   -> JSON {revision, files: {name: {section: {key: value}}}, system: {...}}
apply  <- JSON {revision, changes: {name: {section: {key: value|null}}},
                restart: [unit, ...], system: {hostname?, timezone?, controller?}}
wifi-read, wifi-write, wifi-scan, wifi-action up|down|reset
       -> the Wi-Fi page (admin/wifi.php); see the Wi-Fi section below

Only the configuration files named in pistar.conf are read or written; values
are single-line strings; comments, ordering, ownership and modes are kept.
Every change is written atomically and rolled back, together with the service
restarts, if any step fails.
"""
